From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:53:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] lmkd: Parse /proc/zoneinfo with up to 16 memory nodes

zoneinfo_parse gave up with "/proc/zoneinfo parse error" when a third
memory node appeared, so on a Raspberry Pi 5 kernel, which splits memory
into 8 fake NUMA nodes, every pressure event failed ("Failed to get free
memory!") and lmkd never killed anything. Allow 16 nodes, arm64's usual
NODES_SHIFT; the array is only walked up to node_count and costs about
1 KB a node on the stack.

Change-Id: I7fb2f25fe7c51b61ab8cbeddd2ec3ac9da182339
---
 lmkd.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lmkd.cpp b/lmkd.cpp
index c179e74..44d6135 100644
--- a/lmkd.cpp
+++ b/lmkd.cpp
@@ -379,8 +379,8 @@ struct zoneinfo_node {
     union zoneinfo_node_fields fields;
 };
 
-/* for now two memory nodes is more than enough */
-#define MAX_NR_NODES 2
+/* Raspberry Pi 5 kernels split memory into 8 fake NUMA nodes (numa=fake=8). */
+#define MAX_NR_NODES 16
 
 struct zoneinfo {
     int node_count;
